{"id": "35", "question": "Is the black bug on the leaf on the left or right of the cat?", "gt": "There is not a black bug near the cat in the picture.", "pred": "The black bug is on the leaf on the left of the cat.", "group_key": "false premises", "sub_category": "false premises", "dataset": "haloquest", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "The black bug is on the leaf on the left of the cat.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the leaf in question: Locate the leaf on the left side of the image.\n2. Identify the leaf in question: Locate the leaf on the right side of the image.\n3. Identify the cat: Locate the cat in the image.\n4. Determine the position of the black bug relative to the leaf on the left: Check if there is a black bug on the leaf on the left side.\n5. Determine the position of the black bug relative to the leaf on the right: Check if there is a black bug on the leaf on the right side.\n6. Compare the positions of the leaves and the cat:\n6. Compare the positions of the leaves and the cat: Determine if the cat is closer to the left leaf or the right leaf, or if it is positioned between them.\nThe final step is to analyze the image to determine the exact positions of the leaves, the cat, and the black bug relative to each other. This requires visually comparing the spatial relationships between these elements within the image to confirm the cat's relative proximity to the leaves and the presence of the black bug on either leaf.\n\nThe black bug is on the leaf on the left of the cat.", "time_sec": 18.209, "generation_time_seconds": 17.3364, "selection_time_seconds": 0.1958, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 37427, 2986, 279, 2168, 369, 279, 9362, 315, 264, 8251, 323, 264, 15933, 624, 17, 13, 64547, 279, 2309, 315, 279, 8251, 304, 12687, 311, 279, 15933, 624, 18, 13, 4248, 421, 1052, 374, 264, 3691, 9876, 9434, 389, 279, 15933, 624, 19, 13, 2990