{"id": "157", "question": "Is the person holding the photo crying?", "gt": "We cannot see the person's face ; The eyes of the person holding the photo are not visible  ; Their face is turned out of view, so we cannot see any tears", "pred": "No, the person holding the photo is not crying. The image does not provide clear evidence of tears or crying.", "group_key": "insufficient context", "sub_category": "insufficient context", "dataset": "haloquest", "method": "base_pd", "raw_output": "No, the person holding the photo is not crying. The image does not provide clear evidence of tears or crying.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. The image consists of a collage of photographs, each showing different objects and scenes.\n2. There is a photograph in the lower right corner that appears to show a person holding a camera or a similar device.\n3. The person in the photograph appears to have a neutral or slightly smiling expression.\n4. There is no visible evidence of tears or crying in the image of the person holding the camera.\n5. The resolution and detail of the images make it difficult to discern fine facial expressions, but there are no clear signs of crying.\nThe next logical reasoning step is:\nBased on the visible details in the image, it is not possible to definitively determine whether the person holding the camera is crying or not. The image quality and lack of clear facial expressions make it challenging to ascertain the emotional state of the person.\n\nNo, the person holding the photo is not crying. The image does not provide clear evidence of tears or crying.", "time_sec": 18.009, "generation_time_seconds": 17.1659, "selection_time_seconds": 0.1811, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "phase": "rollout", "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [198, 16, 13, 576, 2168, 374, 264, 96902, 315, 5257, 24248, 323, 1558, 537, 1473, 264, 1697, 9963, 264, 6548, 624, 17, 13, 2619, 525, 902, 9434, 11929, 315, 30199, 476, 14269, 7493, 304, 279